id: pm-zd46m7
title: "GH-1507: Explain effective default list ordering in brief rows and metadata"
description: "Verified on current source: pm list --status open --limit3 --json returns only id status type title, projection.fields matches those four, and sorting reports default/asc. GitHub1507 asks for the actual default ordering keys and visible priority without requiring a second --fields read. Keep the completed explicit-sort fix pm-gh1481 closed and preserve the compact default TOON projection from pm-6pycus. Implement the effective sort contract in the SDK for CLI MCP and extensions with additive compatible envelope metadata."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-19T13:18:41.296Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T09:14:54.966Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-20T09:09:11.462Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-20T09:09:11.462Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Default-sort metadata preserves compatible legacy sort/order fields and exposes an ordered effective-key contract including registry-derived nonterminal-before-terminal grouping, priority ascending, updated_at descending and final ID ascending; Unfiltered lists disclose every comparator stage and the synthetic terminal grouping semantics explicitly; Brief projection includes priority when the effective sort uses it and updates projection.fields and omission receipts accurately; Explicit fields compact and full selections remain authoritative and explicit-sort behavior stays covered; Public SDK CLI MCP and TOON/JSON share the effective policy with configured defaults and stable tie breaking; Focused and packed controls preserve bounded continuation"
parent: pm-srns
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Added priority to default brief rows, declared the four effective status-registry/priority/updated_at/id comparator stages, aligned CLI/runtime/SDK contracts and package dogfood, compacted brief JSON without losing receipts, and independently validated compact and pretty transcript accounting."
expected_result: "Agents can understand the default ranking from brief rows and declared sort stages, retain explicit/custom projections and complete continuation, and trust measured output budgets."
actual_result: "Native and CLI ranking/projection/continuation regressions, independent accounting negative controls, and the real package workflow pass. The unchanged task transcript improves from 13,795 to 13,676 estimated tokens overall; the triage policy costs 67 additional tokens and the specific measured baselines are regenerated. Verification: all four source-identical CI-style coverage shards admitted successfully, then strict Vitest merge and exact covered/total gate pass. 835 test files pass, one configured file skip; 10,829 tests pass and 3 skip. Exact source counts: lines 66,222/66,222; statements 69,828/69,828; functions 14,388/14,388; branches 53,664/53,664. Both linked PM commands pass (author 2 tests, list/accounting/dogfood 170). Four TypeScript configurations pass; real package-first workflow passes; mutation gate has 345 killed plus 7 classified equivalents and zero failures. Graph composition passes the unchanged 1233 prose-gap ceiling; record integrity passes. First-head hosted coverage and all six cold transport budgets pass. Full local static timing failure and launcher lease-wait failures remain recorded separately; no budgets, graph bounds, coverage thresholds or exclusions were weakened. Final exact-head hosted static/smoke/security/analyzer checks and fresh reviews remain required on PR #1517 before merge. CodeRabbit first-head full review has no actionable findings; Sourcery, Greptile and Cubic are unavailable under their recorded free-service limits, not approvals. New source remains Unreleased for the next eligible daily publication."
